Added magic-link login. `POST @magic-link` mails a signed, single-use, short-lived login link; `POST @magic-link-confirm` redeems it for a `jwt_auth` token. Tokens are authlib-signed with a key derived from the same keyring as the flow cookie, burned server-side on first use, capped at fifteen minutes whatever an operator configures, and the send endpoint is rate limited per address *and* per IP. The send answers identically whether or not the address is known, so it cannot be used to enumerate accounts. The resulting `email` identity is verified by construction and counts as a way in for the unlink guard. @ericof
